From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:56:19 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 79/79] runner: an inline span inside an open quotation is
 quoted text, not a cell to own
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The inline trigger fired on `7^222 =` while the model was quoting the request back ("write the line 7^222 =") and
forced the exact value and its mark into the middle of the quotation. The model then read the value as the user's
text, re-quoted it, glued words to the mark and in one reply ran on for 1,024 invented digits. On Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
TP1 (MLX 4-bit, one Spark) the first owned span of 7 of 9 replies in a big-power set sat inside such a quotation.

An inline `<expr> =` or `A mod M =` with an open quotation before it on its line (an odd number of `"`, or a `“`
with no `”`) now abstains with the reason `quoted` (TF_RUNNER_INLINE_QUOTED, default 1; 0 restores the earlier
trigger). Nothing is forced there and no digit stop is armed; the same expression on the model's own line, or after
the quotation closes, is owned as before. runner_api.Abstain is unchanged: the reason is a runner-side hint, because
the server's Decline mirrors Abstain by tag name.

Tests: six new tests under `zig build test-inline-quoted-host` (quoted and curly-quoted requests abstain, closed
quotations and the model's own lines are owned, the knob off restores the trigger, and two recorded TP1 replies).
